---
title: Sheet-pan chicken and potatoes with tahini sauce
servings: 4
tags: [middle eastern, chicken, sheet-pan, weeknight]
source: Sheet Pan Chicken with Tahini-Parsley Sauce by Adrianna Adarme, PBS Food, https://www.pbs.org/food/recipes/sheet-pan-chicken-tahini-parsley-sauce
---

Heat the oven to 350°F.

== Tahini sauce ==

In a #food processor{}, blend the @tahini{1/4%cup}, the juice of a
@lemon{1}, @garlic{2%cloves} and a few pinches of @kosher salt{} until very
smooth.

Add the @Italian parsley{1/2%bunch} and blend until it is finely chopped. With
the motor running, add @water{2%tbsp}(warm, up to 3 tbsp) until smooth. Salt to taste.

== Chicken ==

On a #sheet pan{}, toss the @small potatoes{1%lb} and @green olives{1/2%cup}
with @olive oil{2%tbsp} and a few pinches of @kosher salt{}.

Lay the @chicken{1 1/2%lb}(mixed thighs, breasts and drumsticks) among them.
Drizzle with a little more @olive oil{} and salt both sides.

Roast ~{45%minutes} to ~{50%minutes}, until the skin is crisp and golden.

Scatter with more @Italian parsley{}(leaves) and serve with the tahini sauce
and @lemon{}(slices or wedges).
